    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our lineup leans heavily into the favorable matchups against soft-tossing starting rotations, anchored by the elite 80.26 score for **Jose Caballero**. His high-leverage platoon advantage against Corbin is the catalyst for his ceiling, making him our primary engine for stolen base production. Similarly, **Corbin Carroll** (78.36) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (72.71) are our most potent threats; both benefit significantly from favorable xERA matchups and top-of-the-order protection. While **Josh Naylor** (72.21) faces a manageable arm in Poulin, his power profile remains our safest bet for RBI accumulation in a game projected for high offensive output.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved balancing the middle infield spots, ultimately landing on **Kyle Karros** (54.01) over bench options like **Brice Turang** or **Seiya Suzuki**, who remain sidelined. While **Dalton Rushing** (44.88) and **Alex Freeland** (47.15) occupy the lower end of our starting efficiency scores, their inclusion is forced by the lack of healthy alternatives among our reserves. We are monitoring **Gabriel Moreno** closely; despite a solid score of 65.75, the matchup against Abbott requires high situational awareness, as any late-breaking lineup shifts could render these projections volatile. Our reliance on **James Wood** (63.42) remains high, as his elite xwOBA metrics provide a floor that justifies his start even against the relatively neutral pitching of Hancock.",
